# {{ app_name }}

{{ description }}

This application is organized into four owned areas:

- `data/`: application specification, synthetic-data pipeline, and frozen artifacts.
- `train/`: training configuration, entrypoint, and run artifacts.
- `eval/`: sealed evaluation, evidence, selection, and promotion.
- `src/`: independently installable and deployable runtime.

## Build sequence

1. Complete `BUSINESS_BRIEF.md`.
2. Compile it into `data/specification/application.json`, workflow routes, tool contracts, and acceptance criteria.
3. Set the compiled contract status to `approved` after review.
4. Implement the data pipeline and semantic conversation validator, then run `make data-build`.
5. Configure and run `make train`.
6. Configure the sealed evaluator and run `make eval`.
7. Bind one passing leaderboard entry and its verified artifacts in the release manifest and `eval/results/selected-release.json`, then run `make promote-runtime`.
8. Verify the deployable package with `make test-standalone`.

## Commands

```bash
make help
make install
make validate
make data-build
make train
make eval
make promote-runtime
make test
make test-standalone
make serve
make chat
```

Every pre-build command reports the next required contract or artifact. Application-specific implementations keep these command names stable.

## Runtime

```bash
make install
make serve
```

The HTTP service exposes `GET /health`, `GET /ready`, and `POST /v1/chat`. The initial policy reports that business-policy compilation is ready. Promotion binds the selected policy and application artifacts into `src/{{ package_name }}/`.
